<Base title="Terms of use" description="The rules for using IntoTheTwilightZone.com, its member accounts, forums and fan contributions.">
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <p class="lead">IntoTheTwilightZone.com is an independent, non-commercial fan site and living history of The Twilight Zone. These terms are the ground rules for using it. By creating an account you agree to them.</p>

    <h2>About the site</h2>
    <p>The site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by CBS Studios, Paramount, the Rod Serling estate, or any rights holder. The Twilight Zone is a trademark of CBS Studios Inc. Other trademarks and copyrighted works belong to their owners and are referenced for commentary, criticism and historical documentation. The site earns no money: no advertising, no sales, no affiliate links.</p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must be 13 or older to make an account.</li>
      <li>One person, one account. Keep your passkeys and email secure; you're responsible for what's done with your account.</li>
      <li>Usernames must not impersonate anyone, including cast and crew, rights holders or the site's staff.</li>
      <li>You can delete your account at any time from your <a href="/account/#data">account page</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Community rules</h2>
    <p>Posting in the forums or sharing contributions means following the <a href="/community/guidelines/">community guidelines</a>. In short: be kind, stay on topic, mark spoilers, no spam or advertising, nothing illegal, hateful or sexual, and nobody's private information.</p>

    <h2 id="your-content">Your contributions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You keep ownership</strong> of what you post and upload.</li>
      <li><strong>You give the site permission</strong> to store, display, resize or convert, and link to your contribution on IntoTheTwilightZone.com, for free and worldwide, for as long as it is on the site. You can withdraw an upload or delete a post at any time, which ends that permission (copies already in someone's browser or in backups may take a short while to disappear).</li>
      <li><strong>Only share what you have the right to share</strong>: your own work, public-domain material, openly licensed material (tell us the licence), or material you have permission to share. Do not upload episodes, clips, scripts, scans of books or magazines, music or photos you didn't take unless you have that right. Link to legitimate sources instead.</li>
      <li><strong>Suggestions</strong> you send may be used to correct or add records on the site, written in the site's own words. If you ask for credit, we credit your username.</li>
      <li><strong>Everything is reviewed.</strong> Uploads and suggestions are checked before they appear, and the editor may decline, edit for length or formatting, or remove anything, with or without a reason, though we try to give one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Moderation</h2>
    <p>Moderators can hide posts, close or move topics, reject or remove contributions and suspend accounts that break these terms or the guidelines. Serious or repeated problems lead to suspension. If you think a decision was wrong, use the <a href="/about/#contact">contact details on the About page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Copyright complaints</h2>
    <p>If you believe something on the site infringes your copyright, please follow the steps on the <a href="/copyright/">copyright page</a>. Material under question is taken down while a notice is reviewed. Accounts that repeatedly infringe are closed.</p>

    <h2>No guarantees</h2>
    <p>The site is run by fans, for fans, and is provided as it is. We work hard to get facts right and to source them, but we can't promise the site is error-free or always available. Member posts and contributions are the views of their authors, not of the site. Links to other sites are for convenience; we don't control them.</p>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, the site and its editor are not liable for any loss arising from using it. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under the law where you live that can't be limited.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms as the site grows. If a change matters, we'll say so on the site before it applies. Continuing to use your account after that means you accept the new terms; if you don't, you can delete your account.</p>
  </article>
